      "page_title": "Timeouts: asyncio.timeout, wait_for & wait",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is asyncio.timeout",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async with asyncio.timeout(5):` bounds the whole ==block== (3.11+)",
            "Every await inside shares **one** deadline",
            "`timeout(None)` means no deadline (set one later)",
            "`asyncio.TimeoutError` is an alias of builtin `TimeoutError` (3.11+)"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "    async with asyncio.timeout(5):",
            "        a = await fetch()",
            "        await save(a)",
            "except TimeoutError:",
            "    log(\"too slow\")"
          ],
          "note": "catch it OUTSIDE the async with"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "deadline hits",
                "sub": "loop timer"
              },
              {
                "text": "task.cancel()",
                "sub": "current task",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "CancelledError",
                "sub": "seen inside block"
              },
              {
                "text": "TimeoutError",
                "sub": "raised on exit",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "At the deadline it **cancels** the current task",
            "Inside the block you only see ==CancelledError==",
            "On exit, `__aexit__` converts it to `TimeoutError`",
            "So `except TimeoutError` belongs **outside** the block"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Absolute deadlines",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "end = loop.time() + 10",
            "async with timeout_at(end) as cm:",
            "    await step1()",
            "    cm.reschedule(end + 5) # +5s",
            "    await step2()"
          ],
          "note": "when uses loop.time(), not time.time()"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. wait_for and wait",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "    r = await asyncio.wait_for(",
            "        fetch(), timeout=3)",
            "except TimeoutError:",
            "    r = None  # fetch cancelled"
          ],
          "note": "wraps ONE awaitable only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "On timeout, `wait_for` **cancels** the awaitable",
            "It ==waits== for the cancellation to finish",
            "Then it raises `TimeoutError`",
            "Since 3.12, built on top of `asyncio.timeout`"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "done, pending = await wait(",
            "    tasks, timeout=2,",
            "    return_when=FIRST_COMPLETED)",
            "for t in pending:",
            "    t.cancel()  # your job!"
          ],
          "note": "wait() never cancels anything"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Swallowing `CancelledError` makes the timeout ==hang== or never fire",
            "`except TimeoutError` **inside** the block never matches",
            "Assuming `wait()` cancels the slow tasks: it does not",
            "Passing `time.time()` to `timeout_at`: wrong clock"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Nested timeouts",
          "text": "The **innermost** expiry raises `TimeoutError` first. An outer timeout detects its own expiry through the task's ==cancelling()== count."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The **innermost** expired deadline raises first",
            "Each timeout checks the task's ==cancelling()== count",
            "Its own cancel is undone via `uncancel()`",
            "An outside `cancel()` still propagates as CancelledError"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "bounding await time"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Choosing a Timeout Tool & Nested Deadlines",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Which one?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Covers",
            "On timeout"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`timeout()`",
              "block, many awaits",
              "cancel → TimeoutError"
            ],
            [
              "`wait_for()`",
              "**one** awaitable",
              "cancel, wait, raise"
            ],
            [
              "`wait()`",
              "many tasks",
              "no cancel; (done, pending)"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Nested timeouts",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with asyncio.timeout(10):",
            "    try:",
            "        async with timeout(1):",
            "            await slow()",
            "    except TimeoutError:",
            "        await fallback()"
          ],
          "note": "inner expiry caught, outer keeps running"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Set the deadline later",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with timeout(None) as cm:",
            "    cfg = await load()",
            "    end = loop.time() + cfg.limit",
            "    cm.reschedule(end)",
            "    await run(cfg)"
          ],
          "note": "None = no deadline until rescheduled"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Multi-step job, one budget → ==timeout()==",
            "One slow call, want a value or error → `wait_for()`",
            "Race many, keep the **winners** → `wait(FIRST_COMPLETED)`",
            "Absolute deadline across steps → `timeout_at(when)`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Timeout rules",
          "text": "Catch `TimeoutError` **outside** the block, never swallow ==CancelledError== inside it, and cancel `wait()`'s pending tasks yourself."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "bounding await time"
