    {
      "page_title": "Structured Concurrency: TaskGroup, Fan-out & Queues",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Structured concurrency==: a task's lifetime is bounded by a **lexical** scope",
            "The scope does not exit until all its children finish",
            "Code shape = task tree: indentation shows who owns what"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No **orphaned** tasks: nothing outlives its block",
            "Errors always propagate up to the parent",
            "Cancel the parent → its whole __subtree__ is cancelled"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Origin",
          "items": [
            "Trio ==nurseries== (Nathaniel J. Smith)",
            "Essay: 'Go statement considered harmful'",
            "`TaskGroup` = asyncio's nursery (3.11+)"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: own every task",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def spawn_workers(tg, n):",
            "  for i in range(n):",
            "    tg.create_task(work(i))",
            "async def main():",
            "  async with TaskGroup() as tg:",
            "    spawn_workers(tg, 4)  # owned"
          ],
          "note": "pass tg in, never spawn free"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Helpers take ==tg== as a parameter, not a bare `create_task`",
            "Long-lived services (heartbeat, metrics) → TaskGroup in `main()`",
            "They **shut down** with the app when main's block exits",
            "Blocking/CPU work: `await asyncio.to_thread(fn)` keeps the loop live"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Examples: fan-out & queues",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def get(u):",
            "  async with sem:  # ≤10 at once",
            "    return await fetch(u)",
            "async with TaskGroup() as tg:",
            "  for u in urls:",
            "    tg.create_task(get(u))"
          ],
          "note": "sem = asyncio.Semaphore(10) caps fan-out"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def worker(q):",
            "  while (x := await q.get()):",
            "    await handle(x)",
            "    q.task_done()  # for join()"
          ],
          "note": "None sentinel ends the loop"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "producer",
                "sub": "q.put(item)",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "asyncio.Queue",
                "sub": "buffer"
              },
              {
                "text": "N workers",
                "sub": "in one tg",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "await q.join()",
                "sub": "all done"
              },
              {
                "text": "put None × N",
                "sub": "sentinel",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "tg exits",
                "sub": "clean",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No bare `create_task`: spawn via a ==tg==",
            "**Re-raise** `CancelledError` after cleanup",
            "`shield` sparingly: only commits/payments",
            "Catch group errors with `except*`"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Start N workers **inside** the group",
            "Producer fills the queue, then `await q.join()`",
            "`join()` returns once every item hit ==task_done()==",
            "Send N sentinels; workers return, tg exits cleanly"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
